FEATURE: modal-content-blink
DATE: 2026-10-08
SCOPE: stop the modal content blinking when an open effect ends
FOLLOWS: changelog/modal-slide-effect (uncommitted at the time of this change)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) is the only project affected. No public API changed,
and consumers need no code changes. Apps that symlink vUX (vGet,
app.myinvitees.com, sketch-app) get the fix through their links.

  - vUX-modalDisplayer.js   the animated copy is handed to the host, not rebuilt
  - ChangeLog.md            Fixed bullet

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFECT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reported with a screen recording (modal-blink.mp4) of the modal example using
slideRight. Looked at frame by frame at 30fps: once the slide ended, the sign-in
fields went from autofilled to empty placeholders for about 3 frames (~100ms), then
filled again. The modal's cyan top border appeared at that same moment.

Two causes, both in completeOpen():

  1. When the effect ended, the host was filled with
     `host.innerHTML = layer.sourceOuter`, a new copy built from the markup, and the
     copy that had just animated was hidden. The new copy's inputs were new
     elements: anything typed during the animation was lost, and the browser
     re-applied autofill a few frames later. That was the blink.
  2. The animated copy had its id removed (fillEffectBox), so id-based styles
     (the example's `#loginModal { border-top-color }`) applied only once the
     copy reached the host.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIX
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every effect that animates one whole copy (flip, box, drop, slideLeft,
slideRight) now keeps that copy as layer.liveCopy, with the modal's id on it from
the start. completeOpen() moves that node into the host instead of rebuilding it.
The source has already given up its id before the effect starts, so only one
element in the document has the id at any time.

The closing effects for the same five effects move the displayed node back into
their animation box (reclaimLiveCopy) instead of filling the box with a new copy.
Before this change, the exit animation showed the form with every field empty.

Effects left unchanged:
  - none: no animated copy, so there is nothing to swap.
  - split: animates two half copies that are cleared as they land, so there is no
    single node to hand over. It still rebuilds from markup.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FOLLOW-UP: SIZE SNAP AT THE END OF THE EFFECT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reported with modal-shrink-and-grow.mp4: once the blink was gone, flip and drop
visibly animated at one width and snapped to another when the effect ended. A
first-layer modal got wider and a nested one got narrower.

The animation box was sized from getDimensionOfHidden(source), which returns the
hidden modal's shrink-to-fit width. The host shows the modal at the configured
width (500px by default). openLayer() now measures the modal inside its own host at
that width (measureLayer), so the effect and the displayed modal are the same size.
The mismatch existed before this feature. The blink hid it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FOLLOW-UP: SPLIT HALVES SHOWING THE SAME SIDE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reported with modal-wrong-split.mp4: during split, both halves showed the modal's
left side. Each half's copy was in normal flow, so it was aligned to that half's
left edge. The code set left/right:0 on the copies to anchor them, but that has no
effect on an unpositioned element. Each copy now sits in an absolutely positioned
wrapper anchored to its half's outer edge and as wide as the displayed modal
(fillSplitHalf).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FOLLOW-UP: SPLIT HALVES WITH DIFFERENT AUTOFILL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The halves still did not match: the left half's inputs were white (browser
autofill) and the right half's were not. The browser autofilled only one of the two
copies of the form. Script cannot copy autofill state, so both copies are now made
non-fillable (fields readonly with autocomplete=off, wrapper inert). Split still
rebuilds the displayed modal from markup, so autofill fills it shortly after
landing. This affects split only.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`node --check` passes. Not verified in a browser: the Playwright headless shell
in ~/.cache is missing system libraries (libnspr4, needs sudo to install), WSL
interop is off so Windows Chrome cannot be launched, and jsdom does not run
module scripts. Re-check examples/modal with each effect, with autofilled or
typed fields, in a real browser.
